{# Task-call response-format block for the external-benchmark task modules,
   injected into ``6-task_call.j2`` via the task module's
   ``get_response_format_override()``.

   The benchmark answer is free-form, not a pick from an action menu, so
   the default RULE + ACTION block does not apply. Before this override
   existed the modules' empty ``available_actions`` list was read as the
   NullTask ACCEPT-only sentinel and the agent was told, in the same
   turn, both that ACCEPT was its only valid response and (from
   ``tasks/benchmark/system_rules.j2``) that it must emit ``ANSWER:``.

   Wording is kept consistent with ``system_rules.j2`` so the proximate
   instruction and the system rules agree — including the language: both
   were translated from Korean to English on 2026-09-06 so a benchmark
   cell no longer mixes two languages inside one call. The 2026-09-10
   supervisor-voice revision moved that shared sentence to "exactly like
   this"; the contract itself is untouched.
#}Write your answer on the last line, exactly like this:

ANSWER: <answer>

{{ answer_hint }}
A response with no ANSWER line, or with a differently formatted one, is scored as incorrect.
